.git
.github
**/.vercel
data
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/out
**/.eve
# `eve build` writes `.output` beside `.eve`, and the guest image runs its own
# `eve build`. A local one copied into the context makes that step try to
# rename the existing directory to a backup, which is EXDEV across the overlay
# and fails the whole image. It never reaches a clean checkout because git
# ignores it, so only a deploy from a working tree hits it: exactly the tree
# anyone has after running Eve locally, and exactly when a deploy matters.
**/.output
apps/ios
# Product web is Vercel-only. The guest image is Eve + hub + desk; do not
# ship the Next tree. The Dockerfile drops apps/web from workspaces before
# npm ci, so this exclude is enough (no stub, no COPY of package.json).
apps/web
docs
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
packages/proto/gen/swift
